     "Parsi",
     "Siddi",
     "community"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Over centuries many groups came to India and made it their home. Jews reached the Malabar coast, Syriac Christians settled in Kerala, Parsis fled Persia and settled in Gujarat, and Arab merchants traded on the coasts.\nThe Siddis came from Africa and live in Karnataka and Gujarat. Armenian traders settled in Kolkata and Chennai.\nEach community kept its customs while enriching Indian life with food, language and crafts."
    }
